= Peak live allocation bytes
#text(size: 8pt, fill: rgb("#79542b"), weight: "bold")[Native instruction and allocation measurements · run-20261012T0543Z]

#image("peak-live.svg", width: 100%)

Native primary records retain three repetitions per variant, all eleven inputs, live bytes at entry and the absolute live-byte peak. The graph shows native medians of peak minus the entry value over that same allocation interval. Entry records separate retained inputs and warm outputs from the call's additional peak. No allocation-request, requested-byte, absolute-peak or additional-live-byte regression occurred in primary or paired controls. The complete reduced outputs and retained warm inputs are identical, and the criterion allocation control is unchanged. Process RSS and elapsed runtime were not measured; the host lacks the pressure data needed for controlled timing.

